.TH ZOURCE 1 "2026-11-16" "zource 0.1.2" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
zource \- 2D radial tree and 3D rotating bubble repository visualizer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B zource
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ path | \- ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B zource
visualizes software version-control history and live directory edits as an
animated force-directed graph.
By default it renders directly inside modern graphics-capable terminals
(Kitty, Ghostty, WezTerm, and Foot), including over SSH on headless hosts
where no X11 or Wayland libraries are installed.
When
.B \-w
.RB ( \-\-wayland )
is passed on a system with an active Wayland compositor,
.B zource
dynamically opens
.IR libwayland-client.so.0 ,
.IR libwayland-egl.so.1 ,
.IR libEGL.so.1 ,
and
.I libGLESv2.so.2
at runtime via
.BR dlopen (3)
to render hardware-accelerated 3D spheres in a native
.I xdg_toplevel
window (falling back to
.I wl_shm
shared-memory buffers if EGL/GLESv2 is unavailable).
.PP
Two visualization layouts are available and can be toggled live during
playback with
.BR Tab :
.TP
.B 3D Rotating Bubbles (default)
Directories form nested translucent 3D Fresnel spheres arranged on Fibonacci
orbital shells around their parent directories, enclosing lit 3D file orbs.
Active contributors glide between clusters as glowing orbs and fire additive
beams at files as commits occur.
.TP
.B 2D Radial Tree
Directories radiate outward from the repository root in a 2D force-relaxed
tree with file nodes arranged in phyllotaxis discs around each directory hub.
.SH DISPLAY AND PROTOCOL SELECTION
In terminal mode with
.BR "\-\-protocol auto" ,
.B zource
selects a transport in the following order:
.IP 1. 3
Checks
.BR KITTY_WINDOW_ID ,
.BR GHOSTTY_RESOURCES_DIR ,
.BR TERM ,
and
.B TERM_PROGRAM
for Kitty-protocol terminals
.RB ( kitty ,
.BR ghostty ,
.BR WezTerm ),
or
.B TERM=foot*
for Sixel.
.IP 2. 3
If those variables are absent or generic (for example
.B TERM=xterm\-256color
over SSH), sends a non-blocking Kitty APC graphics query and VT Primary
Device Attributes (DA1) request on
.IR /dev/tty .
Terminals replying with
.B _Gi=31;OK
receive zlib-compressed 24-bit RGB Kitty graphics frames
.RB ( f=24,o=z );
terminals advertising DA1 attribute
.B 4
(such as
.BR foot (1))
receive ordered-dithered 216-color RLE Sixel streams wrapped in DEC Mode 2026
synchronized output.
.IP 3. 3
Otherwise falls back to 24-bit ANSI truecolor UTF-8 half-block
.RB ( \[u2580] )
cells.
.PP
Terminal control and keyboard/mouse input are read from
.I /dev/tty
so standard input remains free for piped event logs.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Display and View Modes
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-terminal
Render inside the active terminal (default).
.TP
.BR \-w ", " \-\-wayland
Open a native Wayland window, falling back to terminal rendering if
.B WAYLAND_DISPLAY
or Wayland client libraries are unavailable.
.TP
.B \-\-wayland\-only
Open a native Wayland window and exit with an error if Wayland is unavailable.
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-protocol " " \fImode\fR
Select terminal graphics protocol:
.BR auto " (default), " kitty ", " sixel ", or " ansi .
.TP
.B \-\-3d
Start in 3D rotating bubble cluster mode (default).
.TP
.B \-\-2d
Start in 2D radial tree mode.
.TP
.BI \-\-size " WxH"
Set pixel resolution cap in terminal mode (default
.BR 960x560 ),
initial window dimensions in Wayland mode (default
.BR 1280x720 ),
or exact frame dimensions for
.BR \-\-output\-ppm .
.TP
.BI \-\-fps " N"
Set target frame rate between 1 and 144 (default: 30 in terminal/PPM mode,
60 in Wayland mode).
.SS Input and Export Sources
.TP
.BI \-\-vcs " kind"
Select version-control or event source:
.BR auto " (default), " git ", " hg ", " custom ", or " live .
In
.B auto
mode,
.B zource
walks parent directories upward from
.I path
looking for
.I .git
or
.IR .hg .
.TP
.B \-\-git
Force Git history ingestion via
.BR git-log (1).
.TP
.BR \-\-hg ", " \-\-mercurial
Force Mercurial history ingestion via
.BR hg (1).
.TP
.BI \-\-log " file"
Read newline-delimited Gource custom log records from
.I file
or standard input when
.I file
is
.BR \- .
Also enabled automatically when standard input is not a TTY and no repository
path was given.
.TP
.B \-\-live
Seed the graph from the working directory and animate live file creations,
modifications, and deletions via Linux
.BR inotify (7).
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output\-ppm " " \fIfile\fR
Render headless binary
.B P6
PPM frames to
.I file
or standard output
.RB ( \- )
for piping into video encoders such as
.BR ffmpeg (1).
Requires no terminal, X11, or Wayland session.
.TP
.BI \-\-max\-frames " N"
Exit after rendering
.I N
frames.
.TP
.B \-\-stop\-at\-end
Exit automatically when historical commit playback reaches the end.
.SS Playback and Appearance
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-seconds\-per\-day " " \fIseconds\fR
Simulation speed in real seconds per repository day (default
.BR 1.0 ).
Smaller values play faster.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-max\-commits " " \fIN\fR
Limit VCS ingestion to the most recent
.I N
commits or changesets.
.TP
.B \-\-loop
Restart from the first event when playback finishes.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-auto\-skip
Disable automatic fast-forwarding across multi-day idle gaps between commits.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-orbit
Disable automatic 3D camera rotation on startup.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-labels
Hide directory and contributor name labels in the scene.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-bloom
Disable radial glow halos around active spheres.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print command-line usage summary and exit.
.SH INTERACTIVE CONTROLS
The following inputs work in both terminal mode (via Kitty keyboard protocol
and SGR mouse reporting) and native Wayland windows:
.TP
.B Space
Pause or resume timeline playback.
.TP
.BR Tab ", " V ", " 2 ", " 3
Smoothly transition between 2D Radial Tree and 3D Rotating Bubbles.
.TP
.B Left\-drag \fRor\fB Arrows \fR/\fB WASD
Orbit camera yaw and pitch.
.TP
.B Right\-drag
Pan camera viewport.
.TP
.B Scroll wheel \fRor\fB Z \fR/\fB X
Zoom in or out.
.TP
.BR + " / " \- " (or " ] " / " [ ")"
Increase or decrease playback speed.
.TP
.BR , " / " .
Seek backward or forward by 5% of total history span.
.TP
.B O
Toggle automatic 3D camera orbit.
.TP
.B L
Toggle in-scene directory and author labels.
.TP
.B B
Toggle radial sphere glow bloom.
.TP
.B R
Restart simulation from the beginning.
.TP
.BR Q " or " Esc
Quit and restore terminal state.
.SH CUSTOM LOG FORMAT
Lines read by
.B \-\-log
follow the pipe-delimited Gource custom log format:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
\fItimestamp\fR|\fIauthor\fR|\fItype\fR|\fIpath\fR[|\fIRRGGBB\fR]
.fi
.RE
.PP
.I timestamp
is Unix epoch seconds (integer or floating-point),
.I type
is
.B A
(added),
.B M
(modified), or
.B D
(deleted), and the optional sixth-digit hexadecimal
.I RRGGBB
field overrides the file's extension color.
Lines beginning with
.B #
are ignored.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B WAYLAND_DISPLAY
Wayland socket name used when
.B \-w
or
.B \-\-wayland
is specified.
.TP
.BR TERM ", " TERM_PROGRAM ", " KITTY_WINDOW_ID ", " GHOSTTY_RESOURCES_DIR
Inspected during
.B \-\-protocol auto
terminal capability detection before falling back to live APC/DA1 probing.
.TP
.B USER
Default author name attributed to working-tree edits in
.B \-\-live
mode.
.SH EXAMPLES
Visualize the current Git or Mercurial repository as 3D rotating bubbles in
Ghostty, Kitty, or Foot:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
zource
.fi
.RE
.PP
Visualize another repository in a hardware-accelerated Wayland window at
0.25 seconds per day:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
zource \-\-wayland \-s 0.25 ~/src/project
.fi
.RE
.PP
Watch live working-tree edits in real time:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
zource \-\-live .
.fi
.RE
.PP
Encode a 60 FPS 1080p MP4 video on a headless server with no display server:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
zource \-\-size 1920x1080 \-\-fps 60 \-\-stop\-at\-end \-\-output\-ppm \- . \\
  | ffmpeg \-y \-f image2pipe \-vcodec ppm \-r 60 \-i \- \-c:v libx264 \-pix_fmt yuv420p history.mp4
.fi
.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Clean exit.
.TP
.B 1
Repository, VCS subprocess, or display initialization failure.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid command-line option or argument.
